  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Given set&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"}\" open=\"{\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>Here sum is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>7</mn></math>&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>24</mn></math></p><p>So there will be two cases</p><p>Case (i) When numbers are&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"}\" open=\"{\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>Arrangement will be&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>_</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>_</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>_</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>_</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#38;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>_</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>_</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>_</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>_</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>6</mn></math></p><p>In unit place&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math>&nbsp;&amp;&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn></math>&nbsp;can take place because for multiple of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn></math>&nbsp;number should be even &amp; sum of digits should be multiple of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn></math>.</p><p>So total way in which remaining number can be taken&nbsp;will be&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo>!</mo><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>2</mn></math>&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>48</mn></math>&nbsp;ways</p><p>Case (ii)&nbsp;When&nbsp;numbers are&nbsp;&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"}\" open=\"{\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>Arrangement will be&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>_</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>_</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>_</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>_</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>2</mn></math>&nbsp;</p><p>So total way in which remaining number can be taken&nbsp;will be&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo>!</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>24</mn></math>&nbsp;ways</p><p>Adding case (i)&nbsp;&amp; case (ii), we get</p><p>required&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn></math>-digit numbers&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>24</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>48</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>72</mn></math></p>",
    "image": null
